  "articleBody": "Loose rugs are often a sneaky culprit when it comes to living room trip hazards. While there aren't any hard deadlines for fixing them, it's a good idea to address them immediately to keep your space safe. So, what's the deal with rugs? You've got a couple of options: you can either remove them completely, especially if they're small and constantly shifting, or you can secure them. If you love your rugs, investing in good non-slip backing or tape is a game-changer. This keeps them firmly in place, even in high-traffic areas. Beyond rugs, take a moment to look at other common trip risks. Are your walkways wide and clear, or do you have furniture or decor encroaching on the path? Cords are another big one – make sure they're not crossing walkways. Instead, route them along the walls or baseboards where they're out of the way. And don't forget about lighting! Adequate lighting, especially for nighttime movement, can make a huge difference in spotting potential hazards. If you have any concerns about modifying your flooring or need help with a more comprehensive home safety assessment, especially if someone in your household has a high fall risk, bringing in a professional can provide that extra layer of confidence and expertise.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
